    {
      "id": "grammar-and-errors",
      "title": "Exact comparisons made progress measurable",
      "phase": 5,
      "metric": "560 → 444 differences",
      "body": "The comparison records the entire parse or check result: whether the program is accepted, where an error occurs, its phase and its diagnostics. Grammar and source-origin repairs closed 116 differences while keeping every previous match and all 919 positive programs. That makes the graph useful for tracking both everyday usability and language behavior.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/rom1504/bend/blob/5350b2fec8f6f8484c7a689e915b359d7ce86847/implementation/phase5/final-conformance.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "representation-and-robustness",
      "title": "Smaller values also made checking more reliable",
      "phase": 11,
      "metric": "1,001 / 1,001 positive accepts",
      "body": "Compact natural numbers and simpler descent eliminated deep-literal failures and a negative-test timeout. Avoiding extra call wrappers then removed a long-string stack overflow under the same resource limits. The exact-match curve moves only four rows across these releases, but those rows represent programs that changed from failing or timing out to the intended result.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/rom1504/bend/blob/5350b2fec8f6f8484c7a689e915b359d7ce86847/implementation/phase9/checker_speed.md",
        "https://github.com/rom1504/bend/blob/5350b2fec8f6f8484c7a689e915b359d7ce86847/implementation/phase11/known_work.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "shared-diagnostics",
      "title": "Shared error rendering improved the developer experience",
      "phase": 15,
      "metric": "603 → 459 differences",
      "body": "One diagnostic renderer restored source carets consistently, and missing-import handling retained the right error context. Together with malformed-binder handling, the release added 144 exact matches without losing an earlier match. These improvements make errors easier to locate and keep the Bend compiler familiar to users of the reference implementation.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/rom1504/bend/blob/5350b2fec8f6f8484c7a689e915b359d7ce86847/implementation/phase15/exact-differences.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "authoritative-origins",
      "title": "Keeping source information early avoided guessing later",
      "phase": 16,
      "metric": "459 → 2 differences",
      "body": "The compiler attached source origins when terms were created and carried them through later transformations. Parser and checker checkpoints also became explicit. This let the compiler select the same error at the same point as the reference, closing 457 differences with no lost matches. Compact literal representation kept this richer information affordable.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/rom1504/bend/blob/5350b2fec8f6f8484c7a689e915b359d7ce86847/implementation/phase16/consolidation.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "contextual-frontend",
      "title": "One contextual frontend closed the remaining gaps",
      "phase": 22,
      "metric": "2 → 0 main; 57 → 0 broader differences",
      "body": "Parsing now carries lexical scope, aliases, namespaces and fresh-name state when they are needed. A shared materializer performs semantic work at the correct early or deferred checkpoint. This replaces reconstruction paths that could choose the wrong error or scope. It closes the final main-suite differences and every remaining difference in the frozen broader selection.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/rom1504/bend/blob/5350b2fec8f6f8484c7a689e915b359d7ce86847/implementation/phase22/contextual-conformance.md",
